# trivy config exclusions for infra/cluster/platform.
#
# Scoped to this directory on purpose. `mise run lint` runs one `trivy config`
# per stack with the stack as the working directory, and trivy reads the
# `.trivyignore` sitting in the working directory, so this file suppresses
# findings in this module and nowhere else.
# https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/
#
# One ID per line, one reason per ID. An entry with no reason is not an accepted
# risk, it is an unread finding, so do not add one.
#
# Nothing else in this module is suppressed, and in particular KSV-0014 is not.
# That finding, the read-only root filesystem on the vLLM container, was fixed in
# the chart rather than accepted: both containers of the inference Deployment now
# set securityContext.readOnlyRootFilesystem, and every path vLLM documents as
# writable is an emptyDir volume. The README section "trivy: one finding fixed,
# one accepted" has the paths and their sources.

# KSV-0125, "Restrict container images to trusted registries".
#
# Two hits, both in charts/llm-eks-inference/templates/deployment.yaml: the vLLM
# server image `vllm/vllm-openai` and the weights-staging init container's
# `amazon/aws-cli`. Neither is on trivy's default trusted-registry list because
# both are Docker Hub repositories.
#
# This is deliberate and it is a decision already recorded: every image this
# cluster pulls goes through the ECR pull-through cache, and the Docker Hub rule
# behind it needs a Secrets Manager credential that is filled in by hand inside a
# cloud window. ADR 0024, docs/adr/0024-ecr-cache-credentials-live-in-a-secret-this-stack-creates.md,
# is the decision and the two-phase apply it implies.
#
# Until that cache is standing, the chart names the upstream repositories, which
# is what trivy sees. The repository is a chart value in both cases, so pointing
# them at the cache prefix is a values change and not a template change. Both are
# pinned by tag, and the vLLM image by digest as well, so what runs cannot change
# under a retag.
#
# Revisit when the pull-through cache is applied with the Docker Hub rule
# enabled: at that point the images resolve from the account's own ECR registry,
# this finding disappears on its own, and this entry should be deleted rather
# than kept.
KSV-0125
